                <pb facs="0745" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">371.1113Keller, W. N.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-11T13:00:00+01:44"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:47
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>56. Department’s December 10, 6 p.m. The report concerning W. N. Keller, an
                    American citizen registered at the Consulate, apparently true. I made a vigorous
                    protest last Friday and the Rumanian Minister for Foreign Affairs yesterday
                    expressed regret and has assured satisfaction following a special investigation
                    being made by a representative of Department of Agriculture [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Justice</hi>] who left here yesterday. Despatch on the
                    situation left today in the pouch.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d647-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
